1c:T466,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Will revoking a permission break the app?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It will not break anything. At most, the dependent feature pauses until you allow it again - a messaging app cannot attach photos while file access is revoked. You can always restore it from the same menu."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which permissions are the most dangerous?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Accessibility, device administrator, display over other apps, and install unknown apps are the most abused, including by scams that read OTP codes and drain bank accounts. Grant them only to apps you know and fully trust, with a clear reason."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why does an app ask for permissions it does not seem to use?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Some are for side features, analytics, or advertising; some developers simply ask for more than they need. Modern Android limits this with one-time grants and picked-file access. Refuse what you do not understand - a good app keeps working."}}]}12:["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-8 py-8","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home (EN)\",\"item\":\"https://cekapk.com/en\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"How to Check App Permissions on Android - and What They Mean in Plain Language\",\"item\":\"https://cekapk.com/en/panduan/cara-cek-izin-aplikasi\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$1c"}}],"$undefined","$undefined",["$","nav",null,{"aria-label":"Breadcrumb","className":"text-sm text-ink/60","children":["$","ol",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1","children":[["$","li","/en",{"className":"flex items-center gap-1","children":[false,["$","$L5",null,{"href":"/en","className":"hover:text-primary-dark","children":"English Home"}]]}],["$","li","/en",{"className":"flex items-center gap-1","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"children":"/"}],["$","$L5",null,{"href":"/en","className":"hover:text-primary-dark","children":"Guides"}]]}],["$","li","/en/panduan/cara-cek-izin-aplikasi",{"className":"flex items-center gap-1","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"children":"/"}],["$","span",null,{"aria-current":"page","className":"font-medium text-ink","children":"How to Check App Permissions on Android - and What They Mean in Plain Language"}]]}]]}]}],["$","header",null,{"children":[["$","h1",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink sm:text-3xl","children":"How to Check App Permissions on Android - and What They Mean in Plain Language"}],"$undefined"]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","p","App permissions are keys you han",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"App permissions are keys you hand to every app: keys to your camera, your contacts, your location, your files, and your microphone. Some are genuinely needed for an app to work; others are demanded by ill-behaved apps to collect data that has nothing to do with their function."}],["$","p","This guide shows how to view and",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"This guide shows how to view and change permissions on an Android phone, explains the important ones in everyday language, and gives a practical rule for deciding which grants are reasonable and which should be revoked."}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","p","To see permissions per app, open",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"To see permissions per app, open Settings, then Apps, choose the app, then Permissions - and change each one any time without deleting the app. You can also review by type: in Settings under Security & privacy, then Privacy, then Permission manager (names vary slightly by brand), pick Location or Contacts to see every app holding it at once. For each permission, apply the function-fit test: does this app's main job plausibly need it? A video editor needing files and camera is reasonable; a calculator needing contacts and location is not - revoke it. Android also offers 'allow only this time' and approximate location - enough for most apps, at far less risk."}],"$L1d","$L1e"]}],"$L1f",false,"$undefined","$L20"]}]
1d:["$","p","In plain terms: Camera and Micro",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"In plain terms: Camera and Microphone mean the app can capture images and sound while allowed - necessary for video calls, dangerous in unclear hands. Contacts means reading names and numbers on your phone - needed by messaging apps, never by games or flashlights. Location ranges from a rough area to an exact point. Storage should mean only the files you pick. Some permissions should make you stop and think: Accessibility, frequently abused by banking scams; Display over other apps; Install unknown apps; and Device administrator. Outside a very clear need, do not grant these."}]
1e:["$","p","Permissions are not a once-in-a-",{"className":"leading-relaxed text-ink/85","children":"Permissions are not a once-in-a-lifetime decision. Apps gain new permissions through updates, and you sometimes grant one in a hurry and forget it. Spend ten minutes every few months in the Permission Manager reviewing Location, Contacts, Microphone, Camera, and Storage. Many brands also provide a privacy dashboard showing which apps recently used sensitive permissions - an unfamiliar name there is your cue to revoke and consider uninstalling."}]
1f:["$","section",null,{"className":"space-y-3","id":"frequently-asked-questions","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"Frequently Asked Questions"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"divide-y divide-mist rounded-2xl border border-mist","children":[["$","details","Will revoking a permission break the app?",{"className":"group p-4","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-ink","children":"Will revoking a permission break the app?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/75","children":"It will not break anything. At most, the dependent feature pauses until you allow it again - a messaging app cannot attach photos while file access is revoked. You can always restore it from the same menu."}]]}],["$","details","Which permissions are the most dangerous?",{"className":"group p-4","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-ink","children":"Which permissions are the most dangerous?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/75","children":"Accessibility, device administrator, display over other apps, and install unknown apps are the most abused, including by scams that read OTP codes and drain bank accounts. Grant them only to apps you know and fully trust, with a clear reason."}]]}],["$","details","Why does an app ask for permissions it does not seem to use?",{"className":"group p-4","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-ink","children":"Why does an app ask for permissions it does not seem to use?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/75","children":"Some are for side features, analytics, or advertising; some developers simply ask for more than they need. Modern Android limits this with one-time grants and picked-file access. Refuse what you do not understand - a good app keeps working."}]]}]]}]]}]
